  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: The menu is grouped by intent (Look up, Understand access, Compare, Review, Change) with foldable groups and a Find a screen box. New: Compare roles, and Business units (the hierarchy as a tree, merging the old Users by business unit). The Cleanup report can remove disabled users from teams and strip their roles, with the usual review and undo. A question-led Home page, a How it works line on every screen, empty states that say what to do, and privilege depths drawn with the Dynamics 365 icons everywhere. Explain access reads only the roles the selected users hold. Compare users always shows the business unit line. 1.1.0: New Explain access (why can this user do this?), What can a user do? (every table against the eight privileges, in the style of the Dynamics 365 security role editor) and Privileged users (roles that can delete across the organization and who holds them). 1.0.1: Packaging update only, no functional changes. 1.0.0: First release. Explore: users and teams, team members, users by role, users by business unit, privilege finder, compare users and a cleanup report. Change: assign roles to users and to teams, manage team membership and clone a user profile; every change is reviewed before it is applied and can be undone.",
